ed beginning of  this year by renzo marcus and his group  they developed a new method to  differentiate human plcs into microclear  and then transplant them into the mouse  brain  this way they are able to study human  microclear cells in their normal  environment  for these analysis they used our adult  brain association kit our antibodies and  most importantly the max quant title  cell sorter which is an instrument for  very gentle  cell sorting that is based on microchip  technology  and in the last paper i want to  introduce you to  the my ultra microscope blaze that i've  also mentioned before in my previous  slides  this fully automated light sheet  microscope can image large or multiple  samples using cutting edge optics  in this publication here they use the  ultra microscope to study the cleared  mouse brain in alzheimer's disease to  quantify plaques and thereby help to  find new approaches to treat this  disease  and  before we come to an end of this  presentation i would also like to  mention shortly our specific products  for the inflamed brain  for several disease models it is  beneficial to also analyze infiltrating  immune cells in addition to the neural  cells and for this we offer the  multi-tissue dissociation kit and the  set of different immune cell microbeads  in the case of eae which is experimental  autoimmune enzyme  encephalomyelitis which is a model for  multiple sclerosis this workflow can  then easily help to isolate and analyze  neural tissue  so here you see an example of isolated  immune cells from a brain of an eae  mouse with our inflamed brain workflow  you can clearly appreciate the different  cell types that are present in the  inflamed brain after the blood brain  barrier got leaky and immune cells were  able to infiltrate the brain  and this workflow can be even used for  the analysis of  immune cells from small tissues like the  spinal cord as you can see here in these  plots  and with this i will come to a summary  of my seco